tengine/godot-proposals/issues/15616, developers could still ensure they aren't rendering outside of the container (just not necessarily as easily, or with all types of content). And even with it, they could still choose to have a container that acts as a portal that extends beyond the bounds of the container\r\n\r\nAnd it's something that could change at runtime. Like in the 3D Endless Runner demo, we support running as a portal (which renders beyond the bounds of the spatial container) and as a volume (which strives to only render within the bounds)","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:24:20Z","updated_at":"2026-10-13T18:39:20Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124382#discussion_r4259880955","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124382","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/4259880955"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124382#discussion_r4259880955"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124382"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/4259880955/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":112,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":8,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/4259960459","pull_request_review_id":5505059458,"id":4259960459,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc796daL","diff_hunk":"@@ -2049,10 +2049,10 @@ void OpenXRAPI::update_head_tracking() {\n \t\t};\n \t}\n \n-\tbool should_submit_spatial_container_layers = false;\n \tif (is_spatial_container_enabled()) {\n \t\tOpenXRSpatialContainerExtension *spatial_container_ext = OpenXRSpatialContainerExtension::get_singleton();\n \t\tERR_FAIL_NULL(spatial_container_ext);\n+\